# Flutter (`mobile/`)

## Structure (feature-first)

```text
mobile/lib/
  app/                 # router, theme, DI overrides
  core/                # api client, errors, secure storage, widgets
  features/<feature>/
    presentation/      # screens, widgets, providers
    domain/            # entities, repository interfaces, use cases
    data/              # DTOs, api sources, repository impls
```

## Locked

- **State:** Riverpod only.
- **API:** typed models + repository pattern; no raw `http` calls from widgets.
- **Tokens:** `flutter_secure_storage` only.
- **Auth UI:** password login (email or username) + Google Sign-In; **no signup screen**.
- **Authz UI:** gate by role; never rely on UI alone — API enforces.
- **Offline:** not in V1 — no sync engines, no local DB as source of truth.
- **A11y:** labels on icon buttons; readable contrast; works phone + tablet.

## Errors

Map API `{ error: { code, message } }` to domain failures; show user-safe messages.

## Tests

- Unit: domain/use cases.
- Widget: login, withdraw confirm, role-gated screens.

```dart
// ❌ BAD — token in prefs, logic in widget
prefs.setString('jwt', token);

// ✅ GOOD — secure storage + provider
await secureStorage.write(key: 'access_token', value: token);
```
